{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr51e6x60dd","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"ceiling test result ls20 frontier synthesis reached 12 of 13 but acceptance gate rejected it","summary":"Dev-time ceiling test: pointed the offline SynthSession at the frontier claude CLI (dev_cli_llm.CliLlm) over the same 13 recorded ls20 transitions qwen-coding failed on. RESULT: the session EDIT produced a program scoring 12/13 (92.3%) after real ANALYZE+PLAN, but FINAL reported \"no program synthesized\" because the single change targeted all indices [0..12] and index 12 (the one ACTION1 that was static / a no-op, the 1-of-9 outlier) did not pass, so the all-or-nothing acceptance gate rejected the whole 12/13 program (adopted=False). Claude correctly hypothesized ls20 physics: the player is a rigid LINKED unit = the color-12 object flood-filled with its adjacent color-9 object; the four actions are pure translations ACTION1=up(-5,0), ACTION2=down(+5,0), ACTION3=left(0,-5), ACTION4=right(0,+5); and everything else (the ~892px color-3 region that reshapes/splits each step, HUD bars) is rendered UNKNOWN so the validator skips it. This SEPARATES the two hypotheses: the harness GENERATION path is sufficient (a strong model threads it to 12/13 with UNKNOWN partial-fidelity), so the qwen failure is largely LOCAL MODEL QUALITY -- but the ACCEPTANCE DESIGN has a real gap: it discards a 12/13 program over one anomalous transition. Recommendation: partial/threshold adoption (accept the best-scoring candidate, or exclude outlier indices from the target set) rather than requiring ALL targets to pass. Two secondary harness findings: (1) a single frontier CLI EDIT completion takes ~450-600s, so the default 120s CliLlm timeout is too tight -- made it EWM_CLI_TIMEOUT_S-overridable, and a full 6x4-attempt session is impractically long (added EWM_CEILING_MAX_CHANGES/RETRIES env caps); (2) the single-shot fallback program died on NameError: 'isinstance' not defined -- isinstance is absent from world_model _SAFE_BUILTIN_NAMES sandbox whitelist, a real gap since synthesized programs commonly use isinstance. All code is DEV-ONLY (bench/ is npm-ignored, modules headed NEVER SHIPS). New test","category":"arc-agi-3","tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T14:36:45.834Z","vec":[-0.03604339063167572,-0.01793554052710533,0.0072641572915017605,-0.03577623888850212,0.07246795296669006,-0.04177441820502281,-0.08295322954654694,0.05547374114394188,0.03143666684627533,0.018676385283470154,0.01847587712109089,-0.047629162669181824,0.030497441068291664,-0.03352229669690132,-0.033914171159267426,0.03541938588023186,0.01786023937165737,-0.03243590518832207,-0.09522084146738052,0.008673078380525112,0.03249174356460571,-0.03453139215707779,-0.028354782611131668,0.03072402998805046,-0.0353243425488472,-0.03979211673140526,-0.06614323705434799,-0.007913817651569843,-0.012320375069975853,-0.09546671062707901,-0.0163338053971529,0.1219005212187767,-0.028512198477983475,-0.04666152223944664,0.040021102875471115,0.03558814898133278,-0.022687209770083427,-0.04351272061467171,-0.060060665011405945,-0.058593716472387314,-0.04190083220601082,0.053232837468385696,0.047478627413511276,-0.04757783189415932,0.03299476578831673,-0.08494936674833298,-0.05352209508419037,-0.07336091250181198,-0.08866310864686966,-0.07186755537986755,0.01507522165775299,0.021119873970746994,0.02775960974395275,0.026320721954107285,0.008968202397227287,0.05096668750047684,-0.0302664116024971,0.011679855175316334,0.01575811207294464,-0.024106154218316078,-0.041322510689496994,-0.0030976964626461267,-0.07088228315114975,-0.0476546548306942,0.04426652565598488,0.012715947814285755,-0.011385375633835793,-0.05068828538060188,0.0034244065172970295,0.05099035054445267,0.009286787360906601,-0.03847000002861023,-0.06560807675123215,0.004847019910812378,0.09503863006830215,0.08315034210681915,0.0663352832198143,0.09270332008600235,0.016695719212293625,-0.12409970164299011,0.020181236788630486,0.007